# META-PREFIX-DECODE: a person's two Escapes, and two Escape bytes in one
# burst, at an idle draft and with a menu open. fx v0.0.16's key decoder
# reads a second ESC before the first's quiet as its meta prefix
# (escape_parser.zig:552-555@481104fd), but its theme monitor, started at
# every launch, sees each byte first: it holds the first ESC and hands the
# second to the decoder at once, and the held one follows on its own 75 ms
# later (theme_monitor.zig:7, :82-93, :150-164;
# app_bootstrap_runtime.zig:481-483). So a burst of two is two Escapes, as a
# person's two presses are: at a draft the second clears it
# (app_input_runtime.zig:2788-2799), and a menu's Escape closes the menu and
# disarms the clear (:2775-2779). `key Escape Escape` is one tmux write, so
# the binary reads both bytes at once; the person's presses are two writes,
# the second sent once the first's hint is on the screen.
# (a) An idle draft, the person's two presses: the draft is cleared.
type alpha one
until shown alpha one
key Escape
until shown esc again to clear
key Escape
until gone esc again to clear
snap a-person-cleared
# (b) The two bytes in one burst: two presses, and the draft is cleared;
# snapped past the clear's 500 ms (gesture_state.zig:4).
type beta two
until shown beta two
key Escape Escape
wait 1
snap b-burst-cleared
# (c) A menu, `/he`'s completions. The person's first press closes it and
# arms nothing; the second, at the draft, arms the clear; the third clears.
key C-u
type /he
wait 1
snap c-menu
key Escape
wait 0.7
snap c-person-closed
key Escape
until shown esc again to clear
key Escape
until gone esc again to clear
snap c-person-cleared
# (d) The menu again, and the two bytes in one burst: two presses, the first
# closing it and the second arming the clear at the draft; a person's press
# 0.3 s later clears it.
type /he
wait 1
key Escape Escape
wait 0.3
key Escape
wait 1
snap d-burst-cleared
